    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2033206329653834233",
      "url": "https://x.com/BigKensyn/status/2033206329653834233",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/BigKensyn/status/2033206329653834233",
      "text": "One thing I will never get tired of doing: giving Rena Wakama her flowers, especially when she deserves every single one.\n\nShe stepped into the head coaching role with very little experience, and like some other Nigerians, I was skeptical about her chances of succeeding with D'Tigress when she was appointed. Right now she's improved a lot, her adjustments, intensity, and leadership have elevated the team to elite levels fast\n\nJust had to say this after watching how Nigeria fought back to beat Philippines. Our game proved she's light-years ahead in this coaching game.\n\nNigeria trailed 42-51 at halftime (down 9), then exploded in the 3rd and 4th quarters, dropping 34 then 25 points, to smash them 101-84. Whatever she told the players at the break lit a massive fire. (Big ups to the squad for executing it too!)\n\nNigeria better start scouting her replacement now. A bigger team is coming to sign Rena soon.\n\nKeep killing it, Coach!\n\n#ballchatwithkenny #fibawwcq",
